The K3 was one of the O'Neill designs, a cylinder 30 km long. 
Would probably make a very nice L-5 colony. 


Nancy Lebovitz, nancy@genie.slhs.udel.edu wrote:

>>The High Priestess: The Environmentalist. Shows a woman
>>sitting between two trees, holding a petition against
>>pollution. 
>
>Yargh! Why give environmentalists a whole card? Why not put
>mix environmentalist symbols with the religious symbols
>on the Hierophant?

Actually, when I invented the new cards, I just looked at the
old cards and used my imagination. It just *felt* right to 
make the High Priestess the Environmentalist. It might have 
been the Isis symbolism. 

Environmentalism isn't necessarily religion, but its tied to 
emotion. The Mage is often seen as Intellect, while the 
Priestess as Emotion. Neither works that well without each 
other. Seen as a single card, the Environmentalist may 
represent New Age fuzzy thinking, the "Save The Seals"-type of 
commericalised environmentalism where people can dampen their 
guilt by saving a few cute animals and protesting. Together 
with the Politician we get a very dangerous form of coercive 
environmentalism. Together with the Transhumanist it becomes 
rational and dedicated to preventing loss of complexity.


>The High Priestess is usually a symbol of hidden knowledge--
>maybe she can be a symbol of "pure science" or math, while
>the Magician is applied knowledge.
>
