On Tue, 15 Nov 1994, Ray wrote:
>    What gets me is these folks, like Chomsky, and that FINS representative
> seem to love democracy except when their cronies aren't in power. 
> Democracy whether representative or direct is supposed to yield this
> great utopia with citizens voting intelligently on concerned issues
> fighting for the socialist ideal. (because if everyone merely
> knew all the facts, they couldn't but help vote socialist, could they?)
> 
>    When this country elects a landslide of republicans and votes
> for bills like Prop 187, they start crying foul. You support a system
> which allows a mob to act against people, don't start objecting when
> a new mob leader is in charge and starts acting against you.

  You have your political systems mis cast.  Locking the people out of 
control over their own destiny, under any form of meaningful 
participatory governance, is the very opposite of regimes that exercice 
control through strategically placed people.  In short, communism, 
socialism, and narrow republicanism belog in the same oppressive class, 
at the opposite pole from democracy.  The outrage expressed by the people 
who are subjected to the politics of rich and poor in this country, has 
been well documented during the past decade or more, and reflects the 
insensitivity of both Republicans and Democrats.  The recent vote 
demolishing the democratic power structure in Congress, to put in Newt 
and his gang, only promises the worst of the worst.

  Vigdor

